import VOA.Examples.TwoSeriesSingTailLift

/-!
# The diagonal slot `r = n` of `BoxInclusion`

For `r = n` the only slot of the tail of `BoxInclusion n r` (`T`-degree `r - N ≥ n`) is `N = 0`,
`T`-degree `n`.  There the test reads `F(J + x̃) ∈ (products of n letters) + (jets of (J + x̃)ⁿ)`,
and everything is homogeneous of polynomial degree `2n` in `u_j, v_j`.  A degree-`2n` element of
the ideal generated by the degree-`2n` jets of `(J + x̃)ⁿ` is a `ℂ`-combination of those jets, so
it comes from a combination `G` of jets of `Tⁿ`; then `(F + G)(J + x̃)` is a combination of products
of letters **with no ideal**, and the letters-only sharpness (`TwoSeriesSingTailLift`, extended
here to polynomials that are homogeneous in the `T`-degree only) forces `F + G = 0`.

* `tDeg k` — the span of the `T`-monomials of degree `k` (any weight);
* `vars_lt_of_free` — the letters-only sharpness for `F ∈ tDeg k`;
* `eq_zero_of_free` — at `N = 0`: `F ∈ tDeg k`, `k ≥ 1`, `F(J + x̃)` a combination of products of
  `k` letters ⇒ `F = 0`;
* `homogeneousComponent_mul_of_isHomogeneous`, `mem_span_of_mem_testIdeal` — the
  degree-`2n` part of the test ideal is the `ℂ`-span of its generators;
* `boxInclusionTail_diag` — **`BoxInclusionTail n n` for every `n ≥ 1`**;
* `boxInclusion_of_le` — **`BoxInclusion n r` for every `r ≤ n`**;
* `twoSeries_gradedUnitary_of_strictModel_singularLift_gt` — the endpoint, with the
  ideal-elimination input `SingularLift n r` needed only for `r > n`.

Everything is proved outright.
-/

